{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.WedderburnArtin","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.SimpleModule.IsAlgClosed","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MaschkeSnSemisimple"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_sum_sq_eq_factorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_sum_sq_eq_factorial","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WedderburnSn.lean#L109-L127","doc":"**RSK sum-of-squares, unconditional.** The Wedderburn block sizes of `K[S_n]` (over an\nalgebraically-closed characteristic-zero field) satisfy `Σᵢ 𝔫ᵢ² = n!`. Proof: `dim_K K[S_n] = n!`\n(free module on `S_n`), and transporting `finrank` across the Wedderburn algebra-equivalence\n`K[S_n] ≃ₐ[K] ∏ᵢ Matrix(𝔫ᵢ)` gives `dim_K K[S_n] = Σᵢ dim_K Matrix(𝔫ᵢ) = Σᵢ 𝔫ᵢ²`. This is the\nidentity `RegularRepBlockTrace.sumSq_dim_eq` obtained only conditionally on `SnWedderburnSpectralData`;\nhere it is outright (no partition labelling of the `𝔫ᵢ` is needed for the sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_block_finrank_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_block_finrank_sq","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WedderburnSn.lean#L99-L107","doc":"**Block `K`-dimensions are perfect squares.** Each block `Matrix (Fin 𝔫ᵢ) (Fin 𝔫ᵢ) K` of the\nalgebraically-closed decomposition has `K`-dimension `𝔫ᵢ²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin_algClosed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin_algClosed","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WedderburnSn.lean#L85-L97","doc":"**Wedderburn–Artin for `K[S_n]` over an algebraically closed field.** When the base field `K` is\nalgebraically closed (and characteristic zero) the division rings collapse to `K`, so `K[S_n]` is\nisomorphic — as a `K`-algebra — to a finite product of matrix algebras `Matrix (Fin 𝔫ᵢ) (Fin 𝔫ᵢ) K`.\nBlock `i` therefore has `K`-dimension `𝔫ᵢ²`. Finite-dimensionality of `K[S_n]` is automatic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin_alg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin_alg","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WedderburnSn.lean#L59-L83","doc":"**Wedderburn–Artin for `k[S_n]`, algebra form.** The same decomposition as\n`sn_wedderburnArtin`, but as a `k`-**algebra** equivalence rather than a bare ring equivalence — the\ndivision rings `𝔇 i` carry compatible `k`-algebra structures. No algebraic closure is needed:\nMathlib's `IsSemisimpleRing.exists_algEquiv_pi_matrix_divisionRing` supplies the algebra form over\n*any* base `R₀` with `Algebra R₀ R`, not only over an algebraically closed one.\n\nWhy this rung matters: the downstream target\n`SnWedderburnPartitionBridge.sn_isotypic_specht_split` is stated as an `≃ₐ[R]`, so the ring-form\n`sn_wedderburnArtin` cannot feed it, while the algebra-form algebraically-closed\n`sn_wedderburnArtin_algClosed` is unavailable over a general characteristic-zero `k`. This theorem is\nthe missing char-0 algebra-form rung between the two.\n\nWhat it still does **not** give (the residual gap in `sn_isotypic_specht_split`): the collapse\n`𝔇 i ≃ k` (ℚ is a splitting field for `S_n`), the partition labelling of the block index, the\nidentification `𝔫 i = dim_k S^{λ_i}`, and the `C₂` block-scalar alignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.WedderburnSn.sn_wedderburnArtin","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/WedderburnSn.lean#L45-L57","doc":"**Wedderburn–Artin for `k[S_n]`.** Over a characteristic-zero field, the symmetric-group algebra\n`k[S_n]` is isomorphic to a finite product of matrix rings over division rings. The block count `N`,\nthe matrix sizes `𝔫 i`, and the division rings `𝔇 i` are produced by the Wedderburn–Artin theorem;\nsemisimplicity is `sn_isSemisimpleRing` (Maschke). ","signatureChunk":0}]}